<section class="method-flow" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="method-flow__inner">
    <header class="method-flow__header section-heading">
      <p class="section-heading__eyebrow">The method</p>
      <h2 id="method-title">From evidence to shared meaning</h2>
      <p class="section-heading__description">
        Authorised source material establishes the evidence base. We publish a candidate model
        for working-group members to examine, challenge and improve. Each review either returns
        the model for revision or, once consensus is reached, moves it forward as a draft
        standard.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure
      class="method-flow__figure"
      aria-labelledby="method-title"
      aria-describedby="method-caption"
    >
      <div class="method-flow__graphic-wrap">
        <img
          class="method-flow__graphic"
          data-method-theme-image
          data-light-src="/images/home/method-loop-light.avif"
          data-dark-src="/images/home/method-loop-dark.avif"
          src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs="
          width="2752"
          height="1216"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <noscript>
          <img
            class="method-flow__graphic"
            src="/images/home/method-loop-light.avif"
            width="2752"
            height="1216"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </noscript>
        <script is:inline>
          (() => {
            const wrapper = document.currentScript?.closest('.method-flow__graphic-wrap');
            const image = wrapper?.querySelector('[data-method-theme-image]');
            if (!(image instanceof HTMLImageElement)) return;

            const wide = window.matchMedia('(min-width: 64.01rem)');
            const forcedColours = window.matchMedia('(forced-colors: active)');
            let request = 0;

            const selectAsset = () => {
              if (!wide.matches || forcedColours.matches) {
                request += 1;
                image.src = 'data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=';
                return;
              }

              const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === 'dark' ? 'dark' : 'light';
              const source = theme === 'dark' ? image.dataset.darkSrc : image.dataset.lightSrc;
              if (!source || image.getAttribute('src') === source) return;

              const currentRequest = ++request;
              const next = new Image();
              next.decoding = 'async';
              next.src = source;

              const apply = () => {
                if (currentRequest === request) image.src = source;
              };

              if (typeof next.decode === 'function') next.decode().then(apply, apply);
              else {
                next.onload = apply;
                next.onerror = apply;
              }
            };

            new MutationObserver(selectAsset).observe(document.documentElement, {
              attributes: true,
              attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
            });
            wide.addEventListener('change', selectAsset);
            forcedColours.addEventListener('change', selectAsset);
            selectAsset();
          })();
        </script>
      </div>

      <ol class="method-flow__text-version">
        <li>People provide source material once, before the review cycle begins.</li>
        <li>Assisted analysis prepares a candidate model and ontology from that evidence.</li>
        <li>OPDA publishes the candidate with its sources, changes and open questions.</li>
        <li>Working-group members discuss, challenge and improve the candidate.</li>
        <li>Requested changes return the candidate to preparation for another pass.</li>
        <li>Consensus exits the cycle and the agreed model becomes a draft standard.</li>
      </ol>

      <figcaption id="method-caption">
        <p><strong>People remain responsible for meaning and decisions.</strong> AI assists with extraction
          and comparison. Working-group members challenge the result, resolve disagreements and decide
          whether it is ready to become a draft.</p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .method-flow {
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .method-flow__inner {
    width: min(100%, var(--content-max));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-7);
  }

  .method-flow__figure {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-7);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-surface-card);
  }

  .method-flow__graphic-wrap {
    width: min(100%, 84rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .method-flow__graphic {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 2752 / 1216;
  }

  .method-flow__text-version {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .method-flow__figure figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .method-flow__figure figcaption p {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .method-flow__figure figcaption strong {
    color: var(--color-text-strong);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 64rem), (forced-colors: active) {
    .method-flow__graphic-wrap { display: none; }

    .method-flow__text-version {
      position: static;
      display: grid;
      width: auto;
      height: auto;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      overflow: visible;
      clip: auto;
      clip-path: none;
      white-space: normal;
      border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      counter-reset: method-step;
    }

    .method-flow__text-version li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: start;
      padding: var(--space-5) 0;
      color: var(--color-text-strong);
      line-height: 1.55;
      counter-increment: method-step;
    }

    .method-flow__text-version li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }

    .method-flow__text-version li::before {
      content: counter(method-step, decimal-leading-zero);
      color: var(--brand-yellow);
      font: 700 var(--text-sm) / 1.55 var(--font-mono);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .method-flow__inner { padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-5); }
    .method-flow__figure { padding: var(--space-5); }
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .method-flow__figure {
      color: CanvasText;
      background: Canvas;
      border-color: CanvasText;
    }
  }

  @media print {
    .method-flow { color: black; background: white; }
    .method-flow__header :is(h2, p),
    .method-flow__figure figcaption { color: black; }
    .method-flow__figure { break-inside: avoid; border-color: black; background: white; }
    .method-flow__graphic-wrap { display: none; }
    .method-flow__text-version {
      position: static;
      width: auto;
      height: auto;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0 0 0 1.5rem;
      overflow: visible;
      clip: auto;
      clip-path: none;
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }
</style>
